  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHAI: Strengthening Accountability for the PeaCe Health programme - Strengthening Accountability for the PeaCe Health programme</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CHAI: Strengthening Accountability for the PeaCe Health programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till den internationella organisationen Clinton Health Access Initiative, CHAI, som ger tekniskt st&#xf6;d till h&#xe4;lsoministeriet i samordning, &#xf6;versyn och rapportering av h&#xe4;lsoprogrammet PeaCe Health under &#xe5;ren februari 2021 till december 2024, liksom st&#xf6;d till s&#xe4;rskilda &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som r&#xf6;r socialt och finansiellt ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande under programperioden.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the international NGO Clinton Health Access Initiative, CHAI, for assisting the Ministry of Health with the coordination, monitoring and management of the PeaCe Health programme during February 2021 to December 2024 with specific measures aimed at strengthening social and financial accountability during the programme duration.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective &#xa0;of the Project is&#xa0;to strengthening accountability and program coordination in the PeaCe Health program through 5 main pathways;

1. Improved People-Centered RMNCAH/N Programme Management and Coordination.
2. Adoption of Integrated People-Centered Health Care Services approach in the provision of RMNCAH/N services and improved Human Resources.&#xa0;
3.&#xa0;Improved Programme Performance, Monitoring and Resource Allocation.
4. Improved Documentation, Dissemination and Learning.
5. Improved Financial Accountability for the PeaCe Health Programme.</narrative>
  </description>
